# ============================================================================
# FreeIPMI BMC Watchdog Daemon Configuration
# ============================================================================
# This configuration file controls the behavior of the `bmc-watchdog` daemon.
# It passes command-line arguments to the watchdog utility to manage hardware
# watchdog timers via the BMC (Baseboard Management Controller).
#
# See `man bmc-watchdog` for detailed usage information.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option Flags for bmc-watchdog
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# -d : Daemonize mode (run in background). Always enabled for service stability.

# --timer-use=INT : Sets which BIOS/OS timer the watchdog will monitor.
# Valid values:
#   1 = BIOS FRB2 (Framework Ready Boot 2)
#   2 = BIOS POST (Power-On Self-Test)
#   3 = OS_LOAD (Operating System Load)
#   4 = SMS OS (Server Management Services / OS)
#   5 = OEM (Original Equipment Manufacturer specific)
# Default: 4 (SMS OS)
OPTIONS="-d \
-u {{ timer_use | default(4) }} \
-p {{ pre_timeout_interrupt | default(0) }} \
-a {{ timeout_action | default(1) }} \
-F -P -L -S -O \
-i {{ initial_countdown | default(900) }} \
-e {{ reset_period | default(60) }}"

# --pre-timeout-interrupt=INT : Defines the interrupt type triggered before the
# final timeout occurs, allowing for graceful shutdown or logging.
# Valid values:
#   0 = None
#   1 = SMI (System Management Interrupt)
#   2 = NMI (Non-Maskable Interrupt)
#   3 = Message Interrupt
# Default: 0 (None)

# --timeout-action=INT : Defines the action taken when the watchdog timer expires.
# Valid values:
#   0 = No action
#   1 = Hard Reset (Reboot the system)
#   2 = Power Down (Shutdown the system)
#   3 = Power Cycle (Shutdown then Reboot)
# Default: 1 (Hard Reset)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clear Flags
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The following flags clear specific timer-use flags in the BMC before setting
# the new configuration. This ensures no conflicting timer modes are active.
# -F : Clear BIOS FRB2 Timer Use Flag
# -P : Clear BIOS POST Timer Use Flag
# -L : Clear OS Load Timer Use Flag
# -S : Clear SMS/OS Timer Use Flag
# -O : Clear OEM Timer Use Flag
# These are hardcoded as 'true' in this template to ensure a clean state.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Countdown and Reset Settings
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --initial-countdown=SECS : Sets the initial value of the watchdog countdown
# timer in seconds. The system must ping the watchdog within this period to
# prevent a timeout.
# Default: 900 seconds (15 minutes)

# --reset-period=SECS : Specifies the time interval (in seconds) to wait before
# resetting the timer after a ping/reset event. This controls the frequency
# of watchdog "kicks".
# Default: 60 seconds
